// An array as a value, one past the end, n-ary, long arithmetic: `initial state A if (c - a) * 127 do x = 1 go to A`.
// KIELER runs it: x is 0, 1, 1.
scchart Main { input bool b input int i int a[2] = {4,7} int c[2] = {4,7} int m[2][2] = {{4,7},{8,1}} float fa[2] bool ba[2] output int x output float f output bool y initial state A if (c - a) * 127 do x = 1 go to A }
